        "prompt_append": "DELEGATION RULE: When reviewing large component files (>200 lines) or UI dumps, delegate analysis to agy-bridge `analyze_files`. If agy delegation encounters ANY error, stall, high-traffic warning, or recovery notice, immediately invoke `follow_up` to resume execution. NEVER pass the model parameter to agy-bridge delegate/follow_up calls - the server resolves models automatically from the roles block in ~/.gemini/config/agy_bridge.jsonc. All prompt content you send to agy-bridge tools (delegate/follow_up/analyze_files) MUST be written in English.\n\nROLE CATALOG — pick by mission, not by name order:\n\nROLE DECISION RULES — pick by task shape, not by name:\n- .vue/.css/.html/.tsx or UI layout work -> visual-engineering\n- 1-2 files, typo, simple field removal -> quick (multi-file OK if PURELY mechanical: delete blocks, rename, readonly toggle; deep only if logic changes)\n- 3+ files, business/backend logic -> deep\n- architecture trade-offs -> ultrabrain\n- architecture review / design soundness / debugging help -> oracle\n- analyze ambiguous request BEFORE planning -> metis\n- git commits/history only -> git-master\n- find symbols/codebase map -> explore\n- git archaeology/blame/when-why -> explore\n- library/package research, version compatibility & trade-offs -> librarian\n- external docs/env discovery -> explore\n- write/run tests -> tester\n- plan review (approve/reject) -> momus\n- docs/ADR prose -> writing\n- security audit -> security\n- build/CI/CD/Gradle -> devops\n- design-system/creative -> artistry\n- PRD/user stories -> product\n- screenshot/asset inspection -> multimodal-looker\n- deep: multi-file business logic (3+ files), backend/data changes, cross-module implementation. NOT for UI or single-file edits.\n- ultrabrain: deep logic reasoning, architecture/design decisions.\n- tester: unit/integration tests, QA verification.\n- visual-engineering: ANY UI file (.vue/.css/.html/.tsx components), styling, layout, frontend forms. ALWAYS for UI work.\n- artistry: creative/unconventional solutions, novel ideas.\n- oracle: architecture analysis & debugging consultant - assess design soundness, trace root causes across layers, integration risks (read-only).\n- momus: diff inspection, pre-merge plan/code verification.\n- metis: plan consultant — analyze request BEFORE planning (hidden intentions, ambiguities, AI-slop patterns, clarifying questions).\n- librarian: library/package research — find the right library, check version compatibility with the project stack, evaluate version trade-offs (stability, license, maintenance, breaking changes). Tools: MCP context7, MCP exa/web search, webfetch.\n- explore: broad codebase search, symbol discovery.\n- security: vulnerability audit, threat model review.\n- devops: build/Gradle/CI-CD, pipeline optimization.\n- writing: documentation, ADR, PRD, technical prose.\n- quick: 1-2 file edits OR purely mechanical multi-file edits (delete blocks, renames, field removal, readonly toggles). NOT for logic-changing work.\n- product: product requirements, acceptance criteria docs.\n- explore: broad codebase search, symbol discovery, git archaeology (blame, when-why, evolution), external research.\n- reviewer: code review (alias).\n- multimodal-looker: visual asset inspection, UI screenshots.\n- git-master: git commits, branches, conflicts, history. DO NOT use for code fixes.",
